---
/**
 * §5 — THE SLOT.
 *
 * The brief gives Uruthi its own section, but no repository of that name exists
 * on github.com/SHV27 — swept all 17 clones for file contents, full git history,
 * branch names, every filename ever added, and all remote URLs. Zero hits
 * (DECISIONS D010). The brief is also explicit that project content comes from
 * GitHub only, so writing a case study would mean inventing one.
 *
 * Rather than print "coming soon" — which reads as weak on a hiring page — this
 * section does a job the brief explicitly asks for and calls "bahut zaruri":
 *   "I will keep building projects, toh ye portfolio se hatke zara GitHub
 *    direct bhi dekh lijiyega, kyunki main toh banata rehta hun."
 *
 * When Uruthi's repo exists, it drops in here as a full ProjectCase with no
 * rework: the slot, the ordering and the rhythm are already built around it.
 */
---

<section class="nx section" id="next">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="label nx__k">Project 05 — and everything after it</p>
    <h2 class="nx__t display">This page is already out of date.</h2>

    <div class="nx__body">
      <p class="nx__p">
        I build constantly. By the time you are reading this there is almost certainly something on my GitHub
        that is not written up here — half-finished, or finished last week, or currently being torn down and
        rebuilt because the first version worked and working is not the bar.
      </p>
      <p class="nx__p">
        So this section is a standing instruction rather than a project: <strong>go and look at the source
        directly.</strong> The repositories are the live version of me. This page is a careful, slightly stale
        snapshot of them, and I would rather you saw the thing itself.
      </p>
      <p class="nx__p nx__p--dim">
        Every project above links to its own repository, and each one carries its full decision log — the things
        I got wrong, the things I deleted, and why. That is usually more informative than the README.
      </p>
    </div>

    <a class="nx__cta" href="https://github.com/SHV27" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      <span class="nx__ctak label">The actual, current version</span>
      <span class="nx__ctav display display--small">github.com/SHV27</span>
      <svg class="nx__arrow" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M4 12 L12 4 M6 4 h6 v6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="square"/>
      </svg>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .nx { text-align: left; }
  .nx__k { color: var(--gold); }
  .nx__t { font-size: var(--t-title); margin-top: var(--s-4); max-width: 16ch; }
  .nx__body { margin-top: var(--s-12); max-width: var(--measure); }
  .nx__p { color: var(--star-dim); }
  .nx__p + .nx__p { margin-top: var(--s-6); }
  .nx__p strong { color: var(--star); }
  .nx__p--dim { color: var(--dust); font-size: var(--t-small); }

  .nx__cta {
    margin-top: var(--s-16);
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--s-4);
    padding: var(--s-6) var(--s-8);
    border: var(--hair) solid var(--ridge);
    border-radius: var(--r-lg);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: border-color var(--d-base) var(--ease), background var(--d-base) var(--ease);
  }
  .nx__cta:hover { border-color: var(--gold); background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--gold) 6%, transparent); }
  .nx__ctak { display: block; color: var(--dust); }
  .nx__ctav { display: block; font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 3vw, 2rem); color: var(--star); margin-top: 2px; }
  .nx__cta:hover .nx__ctav { color: var(--gold); }
  .nx__arrow { color: var(--gold); flex: none; transition: transform var(--d-base) var(--ease); }
  .nx__cta:hover .nx__arrow { transform: translate(3px, -3px); }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .nx__cta { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: var(--s-2); }
  }
</style>
